+         * region rects; fall back to the whole surface when it supplies none.
+         *
+         * Only the most recent frame's regions are retained. A flush may carry
+         * several H.264 frames, and accumulating all their regions would, for
+         * a moving window, suppress everything under the swept path -- leaving
+         * the vacated areas stale. The client draws these frames in order, so
+         * only the last one determines the final state of the H.264 area;
